\"},\"claude-sonnet-5\":{\"inputTokens\":46,\"outputTokens\":6060,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1261270,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":49414,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.765903,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\"}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"fast_mode_disabled_reason\":\"sdk_opt_in_required\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"api_error_status\":null,\"result\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFound the regression in `checkpointBranchDestinations.BranchesFor` in `internal/cli/export.go`. It was checking the session's recorded metadata branch (`Branch`/`checkpointBranch`) first and only falling back to default-branch reachability (`DefaultCheckpointIDs`) when metadata branch was empty. That meant a session whose checkpoint metadata still said `feat/some-branch` kept being filed under `sessions/branches/feat/some-branch/` even after that checkpoint's commit was reachable from the default branch (i.e., merged).\\n\\nPer project history (a matching commit that fixed this exact behavior previously), the intended priority is the opposite: default-branch commit reachability should win first, grouping merged work under `sessions/<default-branch>/`, with the original branch preserved separately as `source_branch`. Metadata branch is only used as the destination when the checkpoint isn't reachable from the default branch (i.e., still unmerged/in-flight).\\n\\nFixed by reordering the checks in `BranchesFor` so the `DefaultCheckpointIDs` reachability check runs first, falling back to the metadata branch only when the checkpoint isn't found there. This is a 2-line reorder \u2014 no other logic changed, and `SourceBranch` was already correctly threaded through `addSelectedSession`/`addSnapshotSession` so provenance is preserved.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- `go build ./...` \u2014 passed\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/...` (full package) \u2014 passed\\n- Also ran targeted subset (`-run 'Branch|Export|Snapshot'`) \u2014 passed\\n\\nNo test files were modified; `go.mod`/`go.sum` untouched.\",\"ttft_ms\":1378,\"ttft_stream_ms\":853,\"time_to_request_ms\":17,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":218208,\"uuid\":\"ada5c43c-3f51-4513-beed-5533f6ff135c\"}\n",
